      <h2 id="step-1-installing-audacity" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 1: Installing Audacity<a href="#step-1-installing-audacity" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Create </strong><code>topics/installing-audacity.dita</code>
      <CodeBlock code={"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<!DOCTYPE task PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Task//EN\" \"task.dtd\">\n\n<task id=\"installing-audacity\">\n  <title>Installing Audacity</title>\n  <shortdesc>Download Audacity from the official website, or install it with your package manager, and launch it once to finish setup.</shortdesc>\n  <taskbody>\n    <prereq>\n      <p>You need about 250 MB of free disk space and an account that can install software.</p>\n    </prereq>\n    <context>\n      <p>Audacity is available for Windows, macOS and Linux.\n      The steps differ by operating system only at the install step.</p>\n    </context>\n    <steps>\n      <step>\n        <cmd>Download Audacity from <filepath>https://www.audacityteam.org/download/</filepath>.</cmd>\n        <info>\n          <p>Select the installer for your operating system.</p>\n        </info>\n      </step>\n      <step>\n        <cmd>Install it.</cmd>\n        <choicetable>\n          <chhead>\n            <choptionhd>Operating system</choptionhd>\n            <chdeschd>How to install</chdeschd>\n          </chhead>\n          <chrow>\n            <choption>Windows</choption>\n            <chdesc>Double-click the downloaded <filepath>.exe</filepath> file and follow the setup wizard.\n            Accept the default location, <filepath>C:\\Program Files\\Audacity</filepath>, unless you have a reason to change it.</chdesc>\n          </chrow>\n          <chrow>\n            <choption>macOS</choption>\n            <chdesc>Open the downloaded <filepath>.dmg</filepath> file and drag Audacity to your <filepath>Applications</filepath> folder.</chdesc>\n          </chrow>\n          <chrow>\n            <choption>Linux</choption>\n            <chdesc>Install from your distribution's package manager, for example <codeph>sudo apt install audacity</codeph> on Ubuntu or Debian, <codeph>sudo dnf install audacity</codeph> on Fedora.</chdesc>\n          </chrow>\n        </choicetable>\n      </step>\n      <step>\n        <cmd>Launch Audacity.</cmd>\n        <substeps>\n          <substep>\n            <cmd>If Audacity asks to scan for audio plugins, click <uicontrol>OK</uicontrol>.</cmd>\n            <info>\n              <p>This happens once, on first launch.</p>\n            </info>\n          </substep>\n          <substep importance=\"optional\">\n            <cmd>Choose <menucascade><uicontrol>Help</uicontrol><uicontrol>Check for Updates</uicontrol></menucascade> to confirm you have the latest version.</cmd>\n          </substep>\n        </substeps>\n        <stepresult>\n          <p>The main window opens with an empty project.</p>\n        </stepresult>\n      </step>\n    </steps>\n    <result>\n      <p>Audacity is installed and ready to use.</p>\n    </result>\n    <postreq>\n      <p>Connect a microphone before you continue to recording.</p>\n    </postreq>\n  </taskbody>\n</task>"} lang="xml" title="topics/installing-audacity.dita" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the new elements</strong>
      <ul>
      <li><code>&lt;prereq&gt;</code> states what must be true before the reader starts. It goes before <code>&lt;context&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;postreq&gt;</code> states what to do after the task is done. It goes after <code>&lt;result&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li>The default HTML5 build shows both sections without a heading. To add the labels "Before you begin" and "What to do next", set the DITA-OT parameter <code>args.gen.task.lbl</code> to <code>YES</code>.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;choicetable&gt;</code> is a step whose action depends on a condition, laid out as a two-column table: <code>&lt;chhead&gt;</code> with <code>&lt;choptionhd&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;chdeschd&gt;</code> for the headings, then one <code>&lt;chrow&gt;</code> per option with <code>&lt;choption&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;chdesc&gt;</code>. It sits inside a <code>&lt;step&gt;</code> after the <code>&lt;cmd&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;substeps&gt;</code> breaks a step into <code>&lt;substep&gt;</code> elements, each with its own <code>&lt;cmd&gt;</code> and optional <code>&lt;info&gt;</code>. Substeps do not nest further; if they would, the step is a separate task.</li>
      <li><code>@importance="optional"</code> on a <code>&lt;step&gt;</code> or <code>&lt;substep&gt;</code> marks it as one the reader may skip. Output prefixes it with "Optional:".</li>
      <li><code>&lt;stepresult&gt;</code> says what happens after one step, as distinct from <code>&lt;result&gt;</code> for the whole task.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;codeph&gt;</code> is inline code: the <code>apt</code> command inside a sentence.</li>
      </ul>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <h2 id="step-2-exporting-audio" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 2: Exporting audio<a href="#step-2-exporting-audio" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Create </strong><code>topics/exporting-audio.dita</code>
      <CodeBlock code={"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<!DOCTYPE task PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Task//EN\" \"task.dtd\">\n\n<task id=\"exporting-audio\">\n  <title>Exporting audio</title>\n  <shortdesc>Export a finished project as a WAV, MP3, OGG or FLAC file that other programs and devices can play.</shortdesc>\n  <taskbody>\n    <prereq>\n      <p>Finish editing and save the project.\n      A project file (<filepath>.aup3</filepath>) can only be opened by Audacity; exporting creates an ordinary audio file.</p>\n    </prereq>\n    <steps>\n      <step>\n        <cmd>Choose <menucascade><uicontrol>File</uicontrol><uicontrol>Export Audio</uicontrol></menucascade>.</cmd>\n        <stepresult>\n          <p>The <wintitle>Export Audio</wintitle> dialog opens.</p>\n        </stepresult>\n      </step>\n      <step>\n        <cmd>Choose a format.</cmd>\n        <choices>\n          <choice>Choose <uicontrol>WAV</uicontrol> or <uicontrol>FLAC</uicontrol> for an archive copy with no quality loss.</choice>\n          <choice>Choose <uicontrol>MP3</uicontrol> or <uicontrol>OGG</uicontrol> for a small file to share.</choice>\n        </choices>\n      </step>\n      <step>\n        <cmd>Set the format options.</cmd>\n        <info>\n          <p>For MP3, the bit rate controls the trade-off between size and quality.</p>\n        </info>\n        <stepxmp>\n          <p>A spoken-word podcast exports well at <uicontrol>128 kbps</uicontrol>, <uicontrol>Mono</uicontrol>.\n          Music needs <uicontrol>192 kbps</uicontrol> or more, <uicontrol>Stereo</uicontrol>.</p>\n        </stepxmp>\n      </step>\n      <step>\n        <cmd>Choose a folder and a file name, then click <uicontrol>Export</uicontrol>.</cmd>\n        <steptroubleshooting>\n          <p>If the <uicontrol>Export</uicontrol> button is disabled, the file name is empty or the folder is read-only.</p>\n        </steptroubleshooting>\n      </step>\n      <step importance=\"optional\">\n        <cmd>Fill in the <wintitle>Edit Metadata Tags</wintitle> dialog and click <uicontrol>OK</uicontrol>.</cmd>\n        <info>\n          <p>Title, artist and album are shown by most players.</p>\n        </info>\n      </step>\n    </steps>\n    <result>\n      <p>The exported file is in the folder you chose.\n      The project itself is unchanged.</p>\n    </result>\n    <example>\n      <title>Exporting a podcast episode</title>\n      <p>Choose <uicontrol>MP3</uicontrol>, set <uicontrol>Bit Rate Mode</uicontrol> to <uicontrol>Constant</uicontrol>, <uicontrol>Quality</uicontrol> to <uicontrol>128 kbps</uicontrol> and <uicontrol>Channel Mode</uicontrol> to <uicontrol>Force export to mono</uicontrol>.\n      A 30-minute episode exports to a file of about 27 MB.</p>\n    </example>\n  </taskbody>\n</task>"} lang="xml" title="topics/exporting-audio.dita" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the new elements</strong>
      <ul>
      <li><code>&lt;choices&gt;</code> is the simpler alternative to <code>&lt;choicetable&gt;</code>: a list of <code>&lt;choice&gt;</code> elements, each one option, when no description column is needed.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;stepxmp&gt;</code> is an example for one step: what the settings look like in a concrete case.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;steptroubleshooting&gt;</code> says what to do if the step does not produce the expected result. It comes last in the step.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;example&gt;</code> is an example for the whole task, with its own <code>&lt;title&gt;</code>. It sits after <code>&lt;result&gt;</code> in the task body.</li>
      </ul>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <h2 id="step-3-removing-background-noise" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 3: Removing background noise<a href="#step-3-removing-background-noise" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Create </strong><code>topics/removing-background-noise.dita</code>
      <CodeBlock code={"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<!DOCTYPE task PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Task//EN\" \"task.dtd\">\n\n<task id=\"removing-background-noise\">\n  <title>Removing background noise</title>\n  <shortdesc>Take a noise profile from a quiet section, then apply Noise Reduction to the whole track to remove hum, hiss and fan noise.</shortdesc>\n  <taskbody>\n    <context>\n      <p>Background noise such as hum from electronics, hiss from a microphone or fan noise degrades a recording.\n      The Noise Reduction effect learns what the noise sounds like from a section that contains nothing else, then removes it everywhere.</p>\n      <note type=\"warning\">This effect changes the audio data.\n      Save the project first; you can undo with <uicontrol>Ctrl+Z</uicontrol> (Windows and Linux) or <uicontrol>Cmd+Z</uicontrol> (macOS).</note>\n    </context>\n    <steps>\n      <step>\n        <cmd>Find a section of the recording that contains only the background noise.</cmd>\n        <info>\n          <p>Look for a quiet gap at the beginning or end.\n          You need at least half a second of noise-only audio.</p>\n        </info>\n      </step>\n      <step>\n        <cmd>Select that section by clicking and dragging in the waveform.</cmd>\n      </step>\n      <step>\n        <cmd>Choose <menucascade><uicontrol>Effect</uicontrol><uicontrol>Noise Removal and Repair</uicontrol><uicontrol>Noise Reduction</uicontrol></menucascade>, then click <uicontrol>Get Noise Profile</uicontrol>.</cmd>\n        <stepresult>\n          <p>Audacity captures the character of the noise and closes the dialog.</p>\n        </stepresult>\n      </step>\n      <step>\n        <cmd>Select the whole track with <uicontrol>Ctrl+A</uicontrol> or <uicontrol>Cmd+A</uicontrol>.</cmd>\n      </step>\n      <step>\n        <cmd>Open <uicontrol>Noise Reduction</uicontrol> again, adjust the settings and click <uicontrol>OK</uicontrol>.</cmd>\n        <info>\n          <p>Recommended starting settings:</p>\n          <ul>\n            <li>Noise reduction: 12 dB</li>\n            <li>Sensitivity: 6</li>\n            <li>Frequency smoothing: 3</li>\n          </ul>\n          <note type=\"caution\">Too much noise reduction makes voices sound metallic or underwater.\n          Start moderate, increase gradually, and use <uicontrol>Preview</uicontrol> before applying.</note>\n        </info>\n      </step>\n    </steps>\n    <result>\n      <p>The background noise is reduced across the whole track.\n      Play it back to check that the voice still sounds natural.</p>\n    </result>\n    <tasktroubleshooting>\n      <p>If the voice sounds hollow after the effect, undo, then lower <uicontrol>Noise reduction</uicontrol> to 6 dB and try again.\n      If the noise is a constant hum at one pitch, the <uicontrol>Notch Filter</uicontrol> effect removes it with less damage to the voice.</p>\n    </tasktroubleshooting>\n  </taskbody>\n</task>"} lang="xml" title="topics/removing-background-noise.dita" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the new elements</strong>
      <ul>
      <li><code>&lt;tasktroubleshooting&gt;</code> is the task-level counterpart of <code>&lt;steptroubleshooting&gt;</code>: what to do when the whole task did not give the expected result. It comes after <code>&lt;result&gt;</code> and before <code>&lt;example&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;note type="caution"&gt;</code> inside a step's <code>&lt;info&gt;</code>, beside the <code>&lt;ul&gt;</code> of settings: a note can share <code>&lt;info&gt;</code> with other blocks.</li>
      </ul>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <h2 id="step-4-preparing-to-record" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 4: Preparing to record<a href="#step-4-preparing-to-record" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Create </strong><code>topics/preparing-to-record.dita</code>
      <CodeBlock code={"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<!DOCTYPE task PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Task//EN\" \"task.dtd\">\n\n<task id=\"preparing-to-record\">\n  <title>Preparing to record</title>\n  <shortdesc>Checks to make in any order before you press Record: input level, sample rate and disk space.</shortdesc>\n  <taskbody>\n    <context>\n      <p>None of these checks depends on another, so do them in whatever order suits you.</p>\n    </context>\n    <steps-unordered>\n      <step>\n        <cmd>Speak at normal volume and watch the recording meter; aim for peaks around -12 dB.</cmd>\n        <tutorialinfo>\n          <p>Leaving headroom avoids clipping, the flat-topped distortion that no effect can repair.</p>\n        </tutorialinfo>\n      </step>\n      <step>\n        <cmd>Set the project sample rate to 44,100 Hz in the bottom-left corner of the window.</cmd>\n      </step>\n      <step>\n        <cmd>Check that the drive holding the project has at least 1 GB free.</cmd>\n        <info>\n          <p>An hour of stereo audio at 44,100 Hz and 32-bit float needs about 1.2 GB.</p>\n        </info>\n      </step>\n    </steps-unordered>\n  </taskbody>\n</task>"} lang="xml" title="topics/preparing-to-record.dita" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the new elements</strong>
      <ul>
      <li><code>&lt;steps-unordered&gt;</code> replaces <code>&lt;steps&gt;</code> when the order does not matter. The children are still <code>&lt;step&gt;</code> elements; output renders them as a bulleted rather than numbered list. Say in the <code>&lt;context&gt;</code> that the order is free, as this topic does.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;tutorialinfo&gt;</code> is additional information for a reader who is learning, as opposed to <code>&lt;info&gt;</code>, which is for anyone doing the step. A stylesheet for expert readers can drop it.</li>
      </ul>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <h2 id="step-5-update-the-readme-and-check-your-work" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 5: Update the README and check your work<a href="#step-5-update-the-readme-and-check-your-work" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Change the "You are on" line</strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/README.md\n+++ b/README.md\n@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@\n \n Build a guide through 27 stages. Maps begin at stage 02; HTML publication begins at stage 03.\n \n-You are on stage 05: inline and block.\n+You are on stage 06: rich tasks.\n \n ## Stages\n "} lang="diff" title="README.md" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Format and check your work</strong> Format the topics:
      <CodeBlock code={"dogsbay-xml format -i topics/*.dita"} lang="bash" />
      <p>Then choose <strong>Project</strong> &gt; <strong>Check Project</strong> in the editor, or run <code>dogsbay-xml check .</code> from the project root. With the lesson's topics in the map (see "Publish your changes"), the output looks like this example:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"health   clean\nbuild    full                 ok  /home/you/audacity-guide/out/full\noutput   clean (full)\nReady: the project is healthy, every deliverable built, and the output of full holds together."} lang="plaintext" />
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <p>The order inside <code>&lt;taskbody&gt;</code> is fixed: <code>&lt;prereq&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;context&gt;</code>, then <code>&lt;steps&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;result&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;tasktroubleshooting&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;example&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;postreq&gt;</code>. To see the validator hold that order, move the <code>&lt;postreq&gt;</code> in <em>Installing Audacity</em> above <code>&lt;result&gt;</code> and check your work. The check names the file and stops. The output looks like this example:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"health   NOT CLEAN\n  invalid: /home/you/audacity-guide/topics/installing-audacity.dita\n  (run project-health for the full report)\nNot ready: stopped at health — the project itself has faults, so nothing was built and no output was read."} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>The <strong>Project Validation</strong> panel, or <code>dogsbay-xml project-health .</code>, gives the line, column, and message. For example:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"Root map: audacity-guide.ditamap (project config); house rules: none (none configured)\nInvalid files (1 of 10):\n  /home/you/audacity-guide/topics/installing-audacity.dita:\n    68:14  error: The content of element type \"taskbody\" does not match its content model.\n\nSummary\n  Invalid files                 1  of 10"} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>Undo the change and check again. Confirm that the check reports <code>Ready</code> before you continue.</p>
      <h2 id="publish-your-changes" class="group scroll-mt-20">Publish your changes<a href="#publish-your-changes" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <p>Add the lesson's topics to <code>audacity-guide.ditamap</code>, then check your work again. The check rebuilds the guide in <code>out/full/</code>. The complete map at this checkpoint is:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<!DOCTYPE map PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Map//EN\" \"map.dtd\">\n\n<map>\n  <title>Audio user guide</title>\n  <topicref href=\"topics/exporting-audio.dita\"/>\n  <topicref href=\"topics/installing-audacity.dita\"/>\n  <topicref href=\"topics/preparing-to-record.dita\"/>\n  <topicref href=\"topics/recording-your-first-track.dita\"/>\n  <topicref href=\"topics/removing-background-noise.dita\"/>\n  <topicref href=\"topics/supported-audio-formats.dita\"/>\n  <topicref href=\"topics/trimming-audio.dita\"/>\n  <topicref href=\"topics/what-is-audacity.dita\"/>\n  <topicref href=\"topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita\"/>\n</map>"} lang="xml" title="audacity-guide.ditamap" />
      <CodeBlock code={"dogsbay-xml check ."} lang="bash" />
      <h2 id="what-you-learned" class="group scroll-mt-20">What you learned<a href="#what-you-learned" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <ul>
      <li>Before and after: <code>&lt;prereq&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;postreq&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li>Inside a step: <code>&lt;cmd&gt;</code> first; then <code>&lt;info&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;tutorialinfo&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;substeps&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;choices&gt;</code> or <code>&lt;choicetable&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;stepxmp&gt;</code> in any order; then <code>&lt;stepresult&gt;</code>, then <code>&lt;steptroubleshooting&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li>After the steps, in order: <code>&lt;result&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;tasktroubleshooting&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;example&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;postreq&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;steps-unordered&gt;</code> for checks in any order; <code>@importance="optional"</code> for steps that can be skipped.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;tutorialinfo&gt;</code> for the learner, <code>&lt;info&gt;</code> for everyone.</li>
      </ul>
